{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>The foreigner's son.</b> These are converts — converts by justice." "<b>Who joins.</b> Past tense verb, and the heh in place of asher, as in <small>ההלכוא אתו</small> (Joshua 10:24)." "<b>He separates me.</b> Patach gadol in place of kamatz katan, and like it <small>כי עתה יאהבני אישי</small> (Genesis 29:32)." "<b>Behold I am a dry tree.</b> Because he does not beget."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 56, :notes {1 "The quoted form ההלכוא preserves the demonstrative heh + participle + locative alef construction Ibn Ezra is explaining."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:59:44.733605661Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}